ESP32 classic (ESP32-WROOM-32 / DevKit V1) - support notes
===========================================================

Status: assessment based on the code (not compiled, not measured on hardware).

Works without changes (pio run -e esp32dev)
-------------------------------------------
- The esp32dev environment already exists in platformio.ini, the code has
  separate default pins for the classic ESP32.
- Audio: I2S DAC on BCK 26, WS 25, DATA 22, or the built-in 8-bit DAC
  (-DSID_OUTPUT_INTERNAL_DAC, GPIO25) - lower quality, no DAC board needed.
- SD card: CS 5, MOSI 23, SCK 18, MISO 19 - uncomment -DPLAYER_SOURCE_SD=1.
- Web panel, serial console (DualSerial handles the missing native USB),
  NVS settings, flash / LittleFS.
- Real SID chip (engine 2): pins 13/14/27/21/32/33, no collision with I2S or SD.

CPU load
--------
- ESP32 and ESP32-S3 both run at 240 MHz; the S3 (LX7) is only slightly faster.
- Plain reSID should fit with headroom (about 38% on the S3; on the ESP32 expect
  a few to a dozen percentage points more - not measured).
- reSID with interpolation (SID_RESID_INTERPOLATE) is too slow on both chips.
- The real load is shown by the "info" command and on the web page.

Main limitation: RAM (WROOM-32 has no PSRAM)
--------------------------------------------
- About 150-200 KB of heap is left after WiFi starts.
- DeepSID is the most demanding source: HTTPS (TLS) takes about 40-50 KB,
  a folder list of up to 1000 entries (MAX_LIST) takes tens of KB, and loading
  a .sid file needs up to 64 KB in one contiguous block.
- With large folders (e.g. /MUSICIANS) and long run time, allocation errors are
  possible. SD and flash sources are safe.
- Possible fixes: a lower MAX_LIST for the ESP32, or a WROVER board with PSRAM.

LCD (ILI9341 + encoder + buttons) - needs changes
-------------------------------------------------
- config.h deliberately stops the build on the ESP32 with #error.
- The current pins (1, 39-42) do not exist on the ESP32 or are unsuitable
  (GPIO1 = UART TX, 34-39 = input only, no internal pull-ups).
- Needed:
  * a new environment esp32dev-lcd,
  * the display on HSPI, e.g. SCLK 14, MOSI 13, CS 15, DC 4
    (collides with the real SID pins 13/14 - LCD + real SID together
    need a different pin map),
  * encoder and buttons e.g. on 32, 33, 21, 16, 17
    (16/17 are used by PSRAM on WROVER modules; 34-39 need external pull-ups),
  * remove the #error in config.h.
- The 320x60 16-bit sprite (about 38 KB) fits in RAM.


